Feature: Mask invoice numbers in purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone

  Background:
    Given the purgo_playground.d_product_revenue table exists
    And the purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone table does not exist

  Scenario: Create a replica of d_product_revenue and apply masking
    Given the table purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone does not exist
    When I create the purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone table as a replica of purgo_playground.d_product_revenue
    Then the table purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone should be created successfully

  Scenario Outline: Mask the last 4 digits of invoice numbers
    Given the invoice_number column in the purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone table
    When masking is applied
    Then the invoice_number should show <masked_result>

    Examples:
      | original_invoice_number | masked_result |
      | 1234234534              | 123423****    |
      | 9823423455              | 982342****    |

  Scenario: Handle incorrect invoice number format error
    Given the invoice_number column contains an incorrect format
    When masking is applied
    Then an error message "Invalid invoice number format" should be produced

  Scenario: Validation for masking operation
    Given the invoice_number column contains numbers with 10 digits
    When masking operation starts
    Then the format should remain 10 characters long

  Scenario Outline: Validate incorrect invoice number length
    Given an invoice number <invoice_number>
    When the length is less than 10 characters
    Then an error message "Invoice number is too short" should be produced

    Examples:
      | invoice_number |
      | 12345          |
      | 678934         |

  Scenario: Verify masking on multiple records
    Given multiple invoice numbers in the purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone table
    When I apply the masking logic to each record
    Then all invoice numbers should have their last 4 digits masked properly

Technical Details:
  Given the Spark version is 3.1.1
  And using Databricks environment
  Validation rules include ensuring column exists, masking is within limits, and accurate masking of only last 4 digits
  Error conditions encompassed:
    - Invalid format check
    - Minimum length check
  Error messages:
    - "Invalid invoice number format"
    - "Invoice number is too short"
